  "info": {
    "description": "Ingests e-commerce orders into a two-stage pipeline: a verbatim **Raw** record first,\nthen a flattened, cleaned **ODS** row written asynchronously by a worker.\n\n## Authentication\n\nEvery endpoint except `GET /health` requires an `X-API-Key` header. A missing or\ninvalid key returns `401`. The key identifies the calling client, and that identity is\nstored with every record it submits.\n\n## What a 200 means\n\n`POST /orders` returns `200` with `status: \"pending\"` once the order has been committed\nto durable storage. From that point:\n\n- **Do not retry.** The order is stored and will be processed.\n- **You need not keep the payload.** It is retained verbatim, exactly as sent.\n- This holds even when the queue is down: the record is already committed and a recovery\n  scan picks it up. Queue health is never the client's problem.\n\nA `200` does not report the **outcome** of processing, which happens afterwards on a\nworker and ends in `processed`, `error` or `duplicate`. Poll `GET /raw/{raw_id}` when you\nneed to know which — acceptance does not depend on it.\n\n### Raw status values\n\n| Status | Meaning | Terminal |\n|---|---|---|\n| `pending` | Accepted and stored, not yet claimed | no |\n| `processing` | Claimed by a worker | no |\n| `processed` | Written to ODS | yes |\n| `error` | Processing failed; see `error_message` | yes |\n| `duplicate` | The `order_id` already exists in ODS | yes |\n\n## What is rejected and what is not\n\nOnly `order_id` is required. **Every other field may be missing, and the order will still\nbe accepted and stored** — incomplete records are flagged for downstream quality\nreporting rather than refused. Unknown fields are preserved verbatim.\n\nTwo things are rejected at the door with `422`: a missing `order_id`, and a value whose\ndeclared type cannot be converted (for example `NaN` in the integer field\n`items[].quantity`).\n\n**Duplicate `order_id` submissions are not rejected.** They are accepted with `200` and\nreach the terminal status `duplicate`. A client that resubmits will not receive a `409`,\nand should not treat the absence of one as confirmation that the order was new.\n\n## Status codes and what to do about them\n\n| Code | Meaning | What the client should do |\n|---|---|---|\n| `200` | Stored; will be processed | Nothing. Poll `GET /raw/{raw_id}` only if you need the outcome |\n| `400` | Replay refused for this record's current status | Do not retry |\n| `401` | API key missing or invalid | Do not retry; check `X-API-Key` |\n| `404` | No record with this `raw_id` | Do not retry |\n| `422` | Payload is invalid | **Do not retry** — the same payload will always fail. Fix it and resend |\n| `429` | Per-client rate limit exceeded | Back off, then retry |\n| `503` | Server busy (connection pool exhausted) | Retry with exponential backoff |\n\nError responses carry a `detail` field. For `422` it is a list of per-field errors; for\nevery other code it is a string.\n\n## Rate limits\n\nLimits are **per authenticated client**, not global — a global ceiling would let one noisy\nupstream deny service to every other one. `GET /health` is unlimited.\n",
    "title": "Order Ingestion API",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "paths": {
    "/health": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "health_health_get",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {}
              }
            },
            "description": "The process is alive. Requires no API key and consumes no rate limit."
          }
        },
        "summary": "Liveness probe"
      }
    },
    "/orders": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "create_order_orders_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OrderIN"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/OrderAccepted"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Stored durably and will be processed; do not retry. The processing outcome is not included — poll `GET /raw/{raw_id}` if you need it."
          },
          "401": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "detail": "Invalid API key"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "API key missing or invalid. Do not retry."
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Payload is invalid: `order_id` is missing, or a value cannot be converted to its declared type (for example `NaN` in the integer field `items[].quantity`). **Do not retry** — the same payload will always fail. Fix it and resend."
          },
          "429": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "detail": "Rate limit exceeded: 60 per 1 minute"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Per-client rate limit exceeded. Back off, then retry."
          },
          "503": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "detail": "Server busy, please retry later"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Server busy (connection pool exhausted). Retry with exponential backoff."
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "APIKeyHeader": []
          }
        ],
        "summary": "Ingest one order"
      }
    },
    "/process_raw/{raw_id}": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "process_raw_process_raw__raw_id__post",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "raw_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Raw Id",
              "type": "integer"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "force",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "default": false,
              "title": "Force",
              "type": "boolean"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProcessRawResult"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Replay dispatched. `triggered` is false when the record was already in a state that needs no replay."
          },
          "400": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "detail": "Cannot force replay a processed record"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Replay refused for this record's current status. `force=true` accepts only `error` and `duplicate`; a `processed` record is never replayed. Do not retry."
          },
          "401": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "detail": "Invalid API key"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "API key missing or invalid. Do not retry."
          },
          "404": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "detail": "Raw not found"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "No Raw record with this id. Do not retry."
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "`raw_id` is not an integer. Do not retry."
          },
          "429": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "detail": "Rate limit exceeded: 60 per 1 minute"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Per-client rate limit exceeded. Back off, then retry."
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "APIKeyHeader": []
          }
        ],
        "summary": "Replay one Raw record"
      }
    },
    "/raw/{raw_id}": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "get_raw_raw__raw_id__get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "raw_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Raw Id",
              "type": "integer"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/RawOut"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "The Raw record and its current status."
          },
          "401": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "detail": "Invalid API key"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "API key missing or invalid. Do not retry."
          },
          "404": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "detail": "Raw not found"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "No Raw record with this id. Do not retry."
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "`raw_id` is not an integer. Do not retry."
          },
          "429": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "detail": "Rate limit exceeded: 60 per 1 minute"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Per-client rate limit exceeded. Back off, then retry."
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "APIKeyHeader": []
          }
        ],
        "summary": "Read one Raw record and its status"
      }
    }
  }
}
